.TH MOX 1 "2026-10-20" "mox 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mox \- parallel OpenCode project orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mox
[--config FILE] [--dry-run] [--run-timeout SECS] COMMAND [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mox turns project ideas into private repositories worked on by isolated
OpenCode agents, and tracks milestones, ETA, human checks and costs of waiting.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [--profile minimal|standard|paranoid]
Write the config and create the projects/cache tree.
.TP
.B plan --ideas FILE [--answers FILE] [--yes]
Ask the planning model for questions and a milestone plan.
.TP
.B up [--target local|vps|auto] [--detach] [--resume] [--retry-failed]
Scaffold, create private repositories and run agents.
.TP
.B status [--watch] [--verbose] [--json]
Show lifecycle, milestone progress, ETA, disk and repo.
.TP
.B milestone start|done|block|todo|list|status [ID]
Update the progress board in the current project.
.TP
.B check [--watch] [--context] [--top N]
Human attention queue; add/done/later/remove/reopen/probe/export/daemon.
.TP
.B vps check|suggest|setup|allow|revoke|approvals|sync|ps|cleanup|plan
Read-only VPS checks, approvals, detached sync and ghost audit.
.TP
.B bot [--once]
Read-only Telegram bot (never run on the VPS unless explicitly allowed).
.TP
.B stats [--json] [--reset --yes]
Cross-project milestone timing calibration.
.TP
.B report [--out FILE]
Markdown report across projects.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/meta-orchestrator/config.toml
.RI (0600),
.I ~/.local/state/meta-orchestrator/
state, plan, checks, stats, events, answers,
.I ~/mox-projects/<slug>/MILESTONES.json
and the private
.I .mox/
tree.
.SH SAFETY
Repositories are always private. Agents get an OpenCode permission config and
PATH wrappers. mox never copies credentials to the VPS and refuses to run its
Telegram bot on a remote host unless explicitly allowed. Detached runs are
recorded and audited with
.B mox vps ps
and
.B mox vps cleanup
.
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/security.md
